<pdd-reason>Decides when technical-question support cards should fire while suppressing noise and repeats.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {"name": "should_fire", "signature": "(utterance: dict)", "returns": "dict"},
      {"name": "reset_call", "signature": "()", "returns": "None"}
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>model_client_python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

<include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

% Goal
Provide a precision-first decision layer that shows cards only for eligible
technical questions and fails closed whenever a safe decision cannot be made.

% Role & Scope
Create root-level `trigger.py`. `should_fire(utterance)` decides whether a
technical support card appears; `reset_call()` begins a new repeat-memory
scope. Use only `model_client.fast_complete()` for model access.

% Requirements
1. Preserve `should_fire(utterance: dict) -> dict`, `reset_call() -> None`, and
   the result shape `{"fire": bool, "question": str, "reason": str}`. Reasons
   are `technical`, `smalltalk`, `repeat`, or `not_a_question`; failures return
   a fresh `{"fire": False, "question": "", "reason": "not_a_question"}`.
2. Evaluate `question → repeat → domain/rewrite`. Reject invalid input, rep
   speech, statements, and back-channels without a model call. Reject a
   current-call repeat before making the single classification/rewrite call.
   Pricing, scheduling, and small talk never fire.
3. Classify `prospect` and `unknown` by content. A prospect's technical
   question fires even when addressed to a colleague; `rep` never fires.
4. When a retrieval-ready technical question fires, immediately remember it
   for the current call. This intentionally treats “fired” as “answered” even
   if downstream work fails, because duplicate suppression has priority.
   `reset_call()` clears that scope.
5. Default repeat matching is normalized, fast, deterministic lexical
   similarity with a clearly named conservative threshold; document that it
   may miss vocabulary-changing paraphrases. Optional mem0 storage is enabled
   by `USE_MEM0`, remains scoped to the call, and falls back to local matching
   on any mem0 failure.
6. Accept model output only when the entire response is a JSON object with
   exactly `fire`, `question`, and `reason`, correct types, an allowed reason,
   and a consistent combination (only `technical` fires). Fences, preambles,
   trailing content, extra keys, and malformed data fail closed.
7. `USE_MOCK=True` uses a deterministic hardcoded classification lookup with
   no model call.
8. Precision over recall governs all classification and repeat thresholds.
   Mark the tuning point in a code comment.
9. Every call prints one line containing
   `[trigger] in=<text> fire=<bool> reason=<reason>`. Render `<text>` as a
   bounded, escaped representation that replaces or escapes newlines,
   terminal controls, and other unsafe characters so user input cannot create
   extra lines or terminal effects.
10. Debug mode adds the stopping gate (`question`, `repeat`, or
    `domain/rewrite`) and reason in one safe line. Escape and bound all
    user-derived log fields and never print model output.
11. The stable labelled fixture below is the accuracy oracle: one flat,
    plainly editable list of `(text, speaker, expected_fire, expected_reason)`
    cases. Run cases in file order with shared call state, score exact `fire`
    and `reason`, require at least 18/20 correct, and independently enforce zero
    fires for every case whose `expected_reason` is `smalltalk` (including
    pricing and scheduling).
12. Offline tests also verify no-model cheap gates, reset isolation, strict
    response parsing, failure containment, and mem0-to-local fallback.

% Dependencies
The preamble supplies frozen interfaces and project-wide constraints.
